          "contentAsciiDoc": "== Synthesis of the Postulate System\n\nThe Counting-Iris Number System rests upon a finite, constructive foundation:\n\n. **Discrete Arithmetic Base (Postulates 0–1, 5, 7)**: Physical reality and mathematical calculation proceed strictly through finite discrete counting steps on multiscale resolution grids \\( \\mathcal{G}_\\omega \\). Continua containing uncountably infinite point-sets are eliminated from linguistic and formal mathematical formulation.\n+\n. **Algebraic Geometry and Clifford Embedding (Postulates 2–4, 9)**: Multivector space \\( Cl(4,1,1) \\) provides the exact geometric container for physical fields, parity dualities, and Spin(2) bivector vortex structures generated by the Iris element \\( \\iota \\).\n+\n. **Observation and Main Scale Projection (Postulates 6, 8)**: Measurement operations over finite observation durations \\( \\tau_{\\text{obs}} \\) map fine vernier readings \\( \\text{Fin}(\\mathbb{R}^{\\ast}) \\) onto standard real flux values via the Main Scale Projection operator \\( (\\downarrow) \\)."
