          "contentAsciiDoc": "== The Aperture Fourier-Iris Spectral Decomposition Theorem\n\n[#theorem-fourier-iris-completeness]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Fourier-Iris Discrete Spectral Completeness\n====\nEvery finite aperture flux function \\( f : \\mathcal{G}_N \\to Cl(4,1,1) \\) expands into a unique, orthogonal finite sum of multivector phase rotation operators \\( \\iota^k \\).\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Aperture Basis Definition**: Define the discrete Fourier-Iris basis operators \\( \\Psi_k(r) = \\iota^{k \\cdot r \\cdot N} \\) for integer harmonic counts \\( k \\in \\{0, 1, \\dots, N-1\\} \\) on partition grid \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\).\n\n. **Orthogonality Relation**: Compute the inner product of basis multivectors using the Iris metric norm:\n\n\\[\n\\langle \\Psi_j, \\Psi_k \\rangle_{\\mathcal{I}} = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{r \\in \\mathcal{G}_N} \\Psi_j(r) \\bar{\\Psi}_k(r) = \\delta_{jk} \\mathbf{1}_{Cl} + \\varpi \\vartheta\n\\]\n\n. **Main Scale Orthogonality**: Under Main Scale Projection \\( (\\downarrow) \\), the nilpotent boundary term \\( \\varpi \\vartheta \\) vanishes, yielding exact discrete orthogonality \\( (\\downarrow) \\langle \\Psi_j, \\Psi_k \\rangle_{\\mathcal{I}} = \\delta_{jk} \\).\n\n. **Parseval Energy Conservation**: The total multivector energy satisfies \\( \\|f\\|_{\\mathcal{I}}^2 = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} |c_k|^2 \\), guaranteeing finite operational energy conservation.\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: Discrete aperture functions on \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\) possess an exact, complete Fourier-Iris spectral representation. \\( \\square \\)\n===="
