          "contentAsciiDoc": "== The Discrete Sobolev Aperture Norm Equivalence Theorem\n\n[#theorem-sobolev-iris-equivalence]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Finite Sobolev Aperture Equivalence in Cl(4,1,1)\n====\nOn discrete grid \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\), the MSRA vernier derivative norm \\( \\|D_{\\mathcal{I}} f\\|_{\\mathcal{I}} \\) is bounded by multivector aperture norms, establishing exact finite Sobolev-type bounds without continuous completions.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Vernier Difference Operator**: Define the MSRA vernier derivative \\( D_{\\mathcal{I}} f(r) = \\frac{f(r + \\delta) - f(r)}{\\delta} \\mathbf{1}_{Cl} \\).\n\n. **Aperture Energy Bound**: Expand \\( D_{\\mathcal{I}} f(r) \\) in terms of the Fourier-Iris basis coefficients \\( c_k \\):\n\n\\[\nD_{\\mathcal{I}} f(r) = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} c_k \\frac{\\iota^{k \\delta N} - 1}{\\delta} \\iota^{k r N}\n\\]\n\n. **Metric Norm Evaluation**: Taking the Iris metric norm yields \\( \\|D_{\\mathcal{I}} f\\|_{\\mathcal{I}}^2 \\le C_N \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} k^2 |c_k|^2 \\), where \\( C_N \\) is a finite rational constant dependent on grid resolution \\( N \\).\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: The discrete Sobolev norm \\( \\|f\\|_{H^1_{\\mathcal{I}}} = \\|f\\|_{\\mathcal{I}} + \\|D_{\\mathcal{I}} f\\|_{\\mathcal{I}} \\) is well-defined and strictly finite for all discrete aperture fields on \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\). \\( \\square \\)\n===="
