          "title": "The Jaynesian Information Conservation Law",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "== The Jaynesian Information Conservation Law\n\n[#theorem-entropy-conservation]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Entropy Conservation in Closed Aperture Systems\n====\nUnder unitary multivector gauge transformations in \\( Cl(4,1,1) \\), the total Jaynesian information entropy \\( S_{\\text{MaxEnt}}(P) = -\\sum_{r \\in \\mathcal{G}_N} P(r) \\ln P(r) \\) of an aperture probability state remains invariant.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Unitary Gauge Action**: Let \\( U \\in Spin(4,1,1) \\) be a multivector gauge transformation satisfying \\( U \\bar{U} = \\mathbf{1}_{Cl} \\).\n\n. **State Density Transformation**: The transformed probability density satisfies \\( P'(r) = P(U r \\bar{U}) \\).\n\n. **Sum Invariance**: Since unitary transformations preserve grid measure \\( \\mu_{\\mathcal{I}}(U \\mathcal{U} \\bar{U}) = \\mu_{\\mathcal{I}}(\\mathcal{U}) \\), the entropy sum satisfies:\n\n\\[\nS_{\\text{MaxEnt}}(P') = -\\sum_{r \\in \\mathcal{G}_N} P(U r \\bar{U}) \\ln P(U r \\bar{U}) = -\\sum_{r' \\in \\mathcal{G}_N} P(r') \\ln P(r') = S_{\\text{MaxEnt}}(P)\n\\]\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: Jaynesian information entropy is strictly conserved under gauge field evolutions in \\( Cl(4,1,1) \\). \\( \\square \\)\n===="
