          "contentAsciiDoc": "== The Iris Minimum Entropy Information Criterion (IMEIC)\n\n[#theorem-imeic-bound]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Exact Model Complexity Bound in Cl(4,1,1)\n====\nThe optimal multivector model complexity for discrete data on grid \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\) is specified by the Iris Minimum Entropy Information Criterion:\n\n\\[\n\\text{IMEIC}(M) = -2 L(\\hat{\\theta}_{\\text{MAL}}) + 2 K_{\\text{grade}}(M) \\mathbf{1}_{Cl}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( K_{\\text{grade}}(M) \\) is the exact multivector grade dimension in \\( Cl(4,1,1) \\).\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Multivector Grade Complexity**: Model space in \\( Cl(4,1,1) \\) is spanned by grades 0 through 6, with total dimension 64. A model \\( M \\) uses \\( K_{\\text{grade}}(M) \\) independent blade generators.\n\n. **Jaynesian Information Loss**: The expected relative entropy (Kullback-Leibler divergence) between the true data generator and model candidate \\( M \\) expands as:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbb{E}_{\\text{MaxEnt}}\\left[ D_{\\text{KL}}(P_{\\text{true}} \\parallel P_M) \\right] = -L(\\hat{\\theta}_{\\text{MAL}}) + K_{\\text{grade}}(M) \\mathbf{1}_{Cl} + \\mathcal{O}(N^{-1})\n\\]\n\n. **Exact Non-Asymptotic Form**: Multiplying by 2 and projecting via Main Scale Projection \\( (\\downarrow) \\) yields the exact criterion \\( \\text{IMEIC}(M) \\).\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: Model selection strictly minimizes information loss without over-fitting multivector grade dimensions. \\( \\square \\)\n===="
