          "contentAsciiDoc": "== The Finite-Sample Cramer-Rao Aperture Inequality\n\n[#theorem-cramer-rao-aperture]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Finite-Sample Vernier Variance Lower Bound\n====\nThe variance of any unbiased operational estimator \\( T(X) \\) for parameter \\( \\theta \\) on discrete grid \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\) satisfies:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Var}_{\\mathcal{I}}(T(X)) \\ge \\frac{1}{I_{\\mathcal{I}}(\\theta)} \\mathbf{1}_{Cl}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( I_{\\mathcal{I}}(\\theta) \\) is the Fisher aperture information multivector norm.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Unbiased Expectation Condition**: Let \\( \\mathbb{E}_{\\text{MaxEnt}}[T(X)] = \\theta \\mathbf{1}_{Cl} \\). Differentiating both sides with respect to \\( \\theta \\) using MSRA derivative \\( D_{\\mathcal{I}} \\) yields:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{x \\in \\mathcal{G}_N} T(x) D_{\\mathcal{I}} P(x \\mid \\theta) = \\mathbf{1}_{Cl}\n\\]\n\n. **Score Operator Identity**: Rewrite \\( D_{\\mathcal{I}} P(x \\mid \\theta) = P(x \\mid \\theta) D_{\\mathcal{I}} \\ln P(x \\mid \\theta) \\).\n\n. **Cauchy-Schwarz Multivector Inequality**: Applying the Iris inner product inequality to \\( (T(X) - \\theta \\mathbf{1}_{Cl}) \\) and \\( D_{\\mathcal{I}} \\ln P(X \\mid \\theta) \\) gives:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbb{E}\\left[ (T(X) - \\theta \\mathbf{1}_{Cl})^2 \\right] \\cdot \\mathbb{E}\\left[ (D_{\\mathcal{I}} \\ln P(X \\mid \\theta))^2 \\right] \\ge \\mathbf{1}_{Cl}\n\\]\n\n. **Fisher Information Identification**: Recognizing \\( I_{\\mathcal{I}}(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}\\left[ (D_{\\mathcal{I}} \\ln P(X \\mid \\theta))^2 \\right] \\) yields the exact lower bound \\( \\text{Var}_{\\mathcal{I}}(T(X)) \\ge I_{\\mathcal{I}}(\\theta)^{-1} \\mathbf{1}_{Cl} \\).\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: No unbiased operational estimator on \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\) can exceed the precision bound imposed by the Fisher aperture information norm. \\( \\square \\)\n===="
