          "contentAsciiDoc": "== Operational Hypothesis Testing on Discrete Grids\n\n[#theorem-operational-hypothesis-testing]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Operational Exactness of Discrete Hypothesis Testing\n====\nLet \\( H_0 \\) and \\( H_1 \\) be operational hypotheses defined on discrete partition grid \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\). The conventional likelihood ratio test statistic \\( \\Lambda(X) = \\frac{P(X \\mid H_0)}{P(X \\mid H_1)} \\) is strictly equivalent to a multivector gauge projection \\( Q_{\\text{gauge}}(X) \\in Cl(4,1,1) \\), wherein conventional \\( p \\)-values represent exact discrete tail-counting aperture fractions under Jaynesian MaxEnt state assignments without continuous integral approximations.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Discrete Tail-Counting Measure**: On finite grid \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\), the operational probability of observing a sample \\( X \\) at least as extreme as \\( x_0 \\) under \\( H_0 \\) is the finite sum \\( p_{\\text{tail}} = \\sum_{x \\in \\mathcal{G}_N : \\Lambda(x) \\le \\Lambda(x_0)} P(x \\mid H_0) \\mathbf{1}_{Cl} \\).\n\n. **Exact Vernier Bounding**: Because \\( \\mathcal{G}_N \\) contains a finite step count \\( N \\), \\( p_{\\text{tail}} \\) is an exact rational step fraction in \\( \\mathbb{R}_{\\mathcal{I}} \\), avoiding continuum normal or \\( t \\)-distribution approximations.\n\n. **Multivector Likelihood Ratio**: Expressing \\( P(X \\mid H_k) \\) in \\( Cl(4,1,1) \\) via Main Scale Projection \\( (\\downarrow) \\) yields \\( \\Lambda(X) \\) as a scalar blade component of the Jaynesian density tensor.\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: Conventional hypothesis testing is an exact finite-aperture tail-counting operation on discrete partition state spaces. \\( \\square \\)\n===="
